{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KttCogastJAekVAooTHccV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tset: Quillbrook Village Hall\n3\trole: governing\n4\tcovers: \"Trustee membership, voting, meetings and decision-making authority\"\n5\t---\n6\t# Trustee Committee Rules\n7\tQuillbrook Village Hall is a fictional organisation.\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Purpose\n10\t1.1 The committee manages the hall for community use.\n11\t1.2 It may hire out rooms and equipment under hall-bookings.md.\n12\t1.3 These rules were adopted on 12 February 2025.\n13\t\n14\t## 2. Committee membership\n15\t2.1 The committee has between five and nine trustees.\n16\t2.2 Trustees must be at least 18 years old.\n17\t2.3 Applicants must live in Quillbrook or a neighbouring village.\n18\t2.4 A trustee serves for two years and may stand again.\n19\t2.5 Trustees receive no payment for committee work.\n20\t\n21\t## 3. Appointment and departure\n22\t3.1 New trustees are elected at the annual public meeting.\n23\t3.2 Election requires more than half of votes cast.\n24\t3.3 The committee may fill vacancies until the next annual meeting.\n25\t3.4 A trustee may resign by giving written notice.\n26\t3.5 Three consecutive missed meetings without explanation trigger a review.\n27\t\n28\t## 4. Meetings and votes\n29\t4.1 The committee meets at least six times each calendar year.\n30\t4.2 Four trustees form a quorum.\n31\t4.3 Decisions require a majority of those present and voting.\n32\t4.4 The chair has a casting vote if votes are equal.\n33\t4.5 Minutes must be approved at the next meeting.\n34\t\n35\t## 5. Spending authority\n36\t5.1 The treasurer may approve routine spending up to £150.\n37\t5.2 Spending above £150 requires a committee vote.\n38\t5.3 Emergency safety spending follows hall-safety.md section 5.\n39\t5.4 Two trustees must approve payments above £500.\n40\t\n41\t## 6. Matters not covered\n42\t6.1 These rules do not set a maximum number of trustee terms.\n43\t6.2 